Directly use the already-visible `numSubFields`, `subFields`, and `offset` members to avoid the redundant `GetNumSubFields()`/`GetSubField()` calls and their duplicate bounds check. This preserves the original fallback and null-subfield behavior exactly.

```cpp
FIT_FLOAT64 FieldBase::GetOffset(const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex) const
{
    if (subFieldIndex < numSubFields)
    {
        const SubFieldBase* subfield = subFields[subFieldIndex];
        return NULL != subfield ? subfield->offset : 0.0;
    }

    return offset;
}
```